{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"2c439c5c4b44461ba1665d0e637497f6767662df181da4922db0efa2a688dbb0","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM config management","key_entities":["REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID","bedrock_model_id","src/rebar/llm/config.py","src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py","docs/env-vars.md","LLMConfig","DEFAULT_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID"],"problem_keywords":["config parsing","unused configuration","dead code","bedrock model id","environment variable"],"propositions":["The config field bedrock_model_id is parsed from environment variable REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID and documented but never read by any consumer code","The Bedrock model id is already correctly carried by cfg.model as a provider-prefixed string bedrock:<inference-profile-id> and parsed via providers.py","Setting REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID produces no observable effect: no model change, no warning, no error, creating silent failure for operators","The knob was introduced in unsubmitted change 1043 and has never shipped, making removal safe with no compatibility impact","Removal is preferred over wiring because cfg.model already provides the correct working path and a second knob would introduce config ambiguity"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787734966832337001,"uuid":"ee8b2c44-1e76-4bac-a7f8-d52f297ff66d"}